; JOB-0084 unattended DUT desktop, derived from the installed NVMe diagnostics.
; Disk layout was verified earlier. HDToolBox remains available in Tools,
; but must not hold up desktop/control-plane startup on every recovery boot.

FailAt 21
C:AddDataTypes QUIET

MakeDir RAM:ENV RAM:T RAM:Clipboards
Assign ENV:    RAM:ENV
Assign T:      RAM:T
Assign CLIPS:  RAM:Clipboards

Assign KEYMAPS:  DEVS:Keymaps
Assign LOCALE:   SYS:Locale
Assign LIBS:     SYS:Classes ADD
Assign FONTS:    SYS:Fonts
Assign ENVARC:   SYS:Prefs/Env-Archive
Assign THEMES:   SYS:Prefs/Presets/Themes >NIL:
Assign IMAGES:   SYS:System/Images DEFER
Assign WANDERER: SYS:System/Wanderer DEFER

C:Mount DEVS:DOSDrivers/~(#?.info)
Path "C:" "SYS:System" "S:" "SYS:Prefs" "SYS:Tools" "SYS:Utilities" QUIET

Copy >NIL: ENVARC: ENV: ALL NOPRO NOREQ PAT "~(def_#?.info)"
Assign THEME:  THEMES:AROSDefault >NIL:
Assign IMAGES: THEME:Images PREPEND >NIL:

; Cold-test the installed AMDGPU build, not an already-resident RAM candidate.
; Remove S:DUT-AMDGPU to return to the diagnostic firmware-display startup.
If EXISTS "S:DUT-AMDGPU"
    Execute S:DUT-AMDGPU
EndIf

IPrefs
Run <NIL: >NIL: QUIET ConClip

If EXISTS "S:DUT-Network"
    Run >T:DUT-Network.log <NIL: QUIET C:Execute S:DUT-Network
EndIf

If EXISTS "WANDERER:Wanderer"
    Run >T:DUT-Wanderer.log <NIL: QUIET WANDERER:Wanderer
EndIf

Echo "DUT: Work stays mounted; Wanderer and this local Shell are available."
C:Shell
